.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt HMM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hmm
.Nd compact terminal wrapper for codex exec
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl m Ar model
.Op Fl p Ar name
.Op Fl c Ar key=value
.Op Fl -host Ar host
.Op Fl -new
.Op Fl -write
.Op Fl -danger
.Op Fl -quiet
.Op Fl -verbose
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -color Ar mode
.Op Fl -no-color
.Op Fl -no-spinner
.Op Fl -instructions Ar text
.Op Fl -no-instructions
.Op Fl -version
.Op Ar prompt
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility runs
the
.Cm codex
command
in JSONL mode and renders the stream as compact terminal output.
It keeps a sticky Codex conversation for the current terminal, accepts prompts
from arguments, standard input, files, or a small in-terminal compose prompt,
and provides short safety presets over Codex sandbox options.
.Pp
With
.Fl -host
or
.Fl -ssh ,
.Nm
still runs locally and instructs Codex to inspect the remote machine through
local
.Cm ssh
commands.
The remote host does not need
.Nm ,
Codex, or
.Cm jq
installed.
Because SSH requires outbound network access,
.Fl -host
runs Codex shell commands with Codex's workspace-write sandbox plus network
access enabled.
The remote machine is still treated as read-only by default through the prompt
instructions.
.Pp
If
.Ar prompt
is omitted and standard input is not a terminal,
.Nm
reads the prompt from standard input.
If
.Ar prompt
is omitted and standard input is a terminal,
.Nm
opens an in-terminal compose prompt.
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
runs Codex with a read-only sandbox.
Use
.Fl -write
to allow workspace writes for one turn, or
.Fl -danger
to bypass Codex approvals and sandboxing.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage information and exit.
.It Fl -new , Fl -reset
Start a fresh terminal session by forgetting the saved Codex thread id.
.It Fl -show
Show the current terminal session id and exit.
.It Fl m Ar model , Fl -model Ar model
Use a Codex model for this turn.
.It Fl p Ar name , Fl -profile Ar name
Use a Codex configuration profile.
.It Fl c Ar key=value , Fl -config Ar key=value
Pass a Codex configuration override.
.It Fl f Ar file , Fl -file Ar file
Read the prompt from
.Ar file .
Use
.Ar -
to read from standard input explicitly.
This option cannot be combined with prompt arguments.
.It Fl -host Ar host , Fl -ssh Ar host
Inspect
.Ar host
through local SSH.
Codex is instructed to run remote commands through local
.Cm ssh
and to treat paths, processes, services, logs, disks, users, and packages as
remote unless the user says otherwise.
.It Fl -write
Allow workspace writes for this turn by setting Codex
.Cm sandbox_mode
to
.Cm workspace-write .
.It Fl -danger
Bypass Codex approvals and sandboxing for this turn.
.Nm
prints a warning unless raw JSON output is enabled.
.It Fl -quiet
Print only assistant messages.
.It Fl -verbose
Show extra renderer event details.
.It Fl -json
Print raw Codex JSONL events.
This disables color and the thinking indicator.
.It Fl -color Ar mode
Set color mode.
.Ar mode
must be
.Cm auto ,
.Cm always ,
or
.Cm never .
.It Fl -no-color
Disable color and text styling.
.It Fl -no-spinner
Disable the thinking indicator.
.It Fl -instructions Ar text
Override the default instruction prefix for this turn.
.It Fl -no-instructions
Send the prompt without the default instruction prefix.
.It Fl -version
Show the
.Nm
version and exit.
.It Fl -enable Ar name , Fl -disable Ar name
Pass a Codex feature toggle option.
.It Fl i Ar path , Fl -image Ar path
Pass an image path to Codex.
.It Fl C Ar dir , Fl -cd Ar dir
Pass a working directory to Codex.
.It Fl -add-dir Ar dir
Pass an additional writable or readable directory to Codex.
.It Fl -local-provider Ar name
Pass a local provider name to Codex.
.It Fl -output-schema Ar schema
Pass an output schema to Codex.
.It Fl -strict-config
Pass Codex strict configuration mode.
.It Fl -oss
Pass Codex OSS mode.
.It Fl -ignore-user-config
Tell Codex to ignore user configuration.
.It Fl -ignore-rules
Tell Codex to ignore repository rules.
.It Fl -dangerously-bypass-hook-trust
Pass Codex hook trust bypass mode.
.It Fl -
Stop option parsing.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev HMM_INSTRUCTIONS
Default instruction prefix prepended to prompts.
.It Ev HMM_LIBEXEC
Directory containing private helper executables.
.It Ev HMM_STATE_DIR
Directory for session state.
The default is
.Pa ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/hmm .
.It Ev HMM_SHELL_PID
Override the shell process id used to compute the terminal session key.
.It Ev HMM_TTY
Override the terminal path used to compute the terminal session key.
.It Ev TMPDIR
Directory for temporary files.
.It Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for state files when
.Ev HMM_STATE_DIR
is not set.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/hmm/sessions
Default directory for per-terminal Codex thread ids.
Remote host sessions are keyed separately from local sessions.
.It Pa libexec/hmm-codex
Private helper that invokes the
.Cm codex
command.
.It Pa libexec/hmm-render
Private JSONL renderer.
.It Pa libexec/hmm-session
Private session state helper.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
If Codex exits with a non-zero status,
.Nm
exits with that status.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Ask a short question:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hmm "how do I flush DNS cache on macOS?"
.Ed
.Pp
Send a multiline prompt with a heredoc:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hmm <<'EOF'
Explain `find . -name "*.log" -mtime +7 -delete`.
EOF
.Ed
.Pp
Allow workspace writes for one turn:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hmm --write "create a tarball of this directory"
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect a remote host over SSH:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hmm --host m@my-nas "list what's in my downloads dir"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
The
.Cm codex
command,
and the
.Cm ssh
command.
